# Layout 5 — Single-column document (Notion style)

No cards, no grid. One readable column: title, labels as chips under it, properties as inline rows (relations are just another property), divider, annotations. Versions live in a header dropdown.

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Tools / Hammer drill                            [v3 Draft ▾]  [Publish] [⋮]      │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                                  │
│      Hammer drill                                                                │
│      ◉ equipment  ◉ heavy  ◉ rental  [+]                                         │
│                                                                                  │
│      Power         1100 W                                                        │
│      Weight        2.9 kg                                                        │
│      Description   Long text reads like a document at comfortable                │
│                    measure, wrapping naturally.                                  │
│      kit of        → Site kit A                                                  │
│      stored in     ← Depot 7 [v2]                                                │
│      ▸ 2 empty properties                                                        │
│                                                                                  │
│      ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────                    │
│      Notes │ Tasks │ Activity                                                    │
│                                                                                  │
│      ▸ "Check chuck wear" — Kalle · 2d                                           │
│      ▸ ☐ Order spare batteries · due Fri                                         │
│                                                                                  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

```
[v3 Draft ▾] dropdown:          ┌────────────────────┐
                                │ ● v3 Draft         │
                                │ ○ v2 Latest        │
                                │ ○ v1               │
                                │ ── New version ──  │
                                └────────────────────┘
```

**Pros:** calmest read; relations unified into the property list (one mental model); versions out of the way until needed.
**Cons:** version state less visible (buried in dropdown); long relation lists awkward as property rows; everything below the fold w/ many fields.
**Best when:** instances read like records/specs; version ops are rare.
